<title>USA: Coach USA Inc Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Coach USA Inc Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pro forma Combined Statements of Income</p>
<p>For the three months ended March 31, 1997 &amp; 1996</p>
<p>(Unaudited - In thousands except for EPS)</p>
<p>					   Three Months Ended</p>
<p>				 3/31/97	 %	3/31/96	%</p>
<p> Revenues		    $ 69,311  100.0%    $ 52,515  100.0%</p>
<p> Merger costs - poolings (1)  117    0.2%	   ---    0.0%</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary</p>
<p>  items			   2,033    2.9%	   816    1.6%</p>
<p>Extraordinary items (net of</p>
<p>  income taxes)		  (89)		     ---</p>
<p> Net Income		     1,944		     816</p>
<p> Weighted Avg. Shares	18,152		  13,372</p>
<p> EPS (1)			   0.12		    0.06</p>
<p> Depreciation		   4,822		   3,283</p>
<p> Amortization		     466			96</p>
<p> EBITDA			  12,082   17.4%	 6,994   13.3%</p>
<p>Note 1:  The above pro forma net income for the 1997 period includes non-recurring costs associated with certain 1997 pooling-of-interests transactions to acquisitions. The extraordinary items for the quarter are the result of early extinguishments of debt.</p>
<p>2: On May 17, 1996, Coach USA acquired six motorcoach businesses, simultaneously with the closing of its initial public offering.  Additionally, the company made 14 acquisitions using both purchase and pooling-of-interests accounting in August and December 1996 and in February 1997.</p>
<p>3:  Prior to the Mergers, the founding and pooled companies have been managed as independent private companies.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
